FerrionOS change to upstream RedoxFS (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 5ba45a6887374ab425326656a276bb3b62eba7dc after the existing recipe patches. Found by the deterministic simulation in sim/redoxfs (sim/redoxfs/run.sh replay FILE runs a replay).

Formatting a used disk was not crash safe: the header ring was erased in slot order, so a power loss could leave an older, stale header of the old volume as the newest one, and the new volume was built in three commits after a header without a tree, so a power loss could leave a volume that mounts without a tree or root directory. Old headers are now erased oldest generation first with a flush after each, no header is written before the first commit, and the tree, allocator and root directory are created in that one commit.

Replay: 400 writes, then a power loss after 258 (or 262) writes of a reformat mounts a volume whose walk fails (or that leaks a block).
